-- title:
--   Truncated formal group law as a finite Hopf algebra, nilpotent case
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $d\in\mathbb N$, and let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $A$: a family $\Phi_i\in A[\![X_j,Y_j]\!]$ ($i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$) with zero constant term, with linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each of the two groups of variables, and satisfying the associativity identity; assume $\Phi$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two groups of variables fixes each $\Phi_i$. Let $n\in\mathbb N$ and let $\Phi.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,n$ be the $n$-fold iterate defined by $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,0=0$ and $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,(n+1)_i=\Phi_i(\mathrm{nthSeries}\,n,\,X)$, a $d$-tuple in $A[\![X_1,\dots,X_d]\!]$. Assume the quotient $Q:=A[\![X]\!]/I$ by the ideal $I$ generated by these $d$ series is finite and free as an $A$-module, and that the class of each $X_i$ in $Q$ is nilpotent. Then there exist a type $L$ carrying a commutative ring structure, a Hopf $A$-algebra structure whose comultiplication is cocommutative, and free and finite as an $A$-module, together with a surjective $A$-algebra map $\pi\colon A[\![X]\!]\to L$ with $\ker\pi=I$, with $\mathrm{finrank}_A L=\mathrm{finrank}_A Q$, such that each $\pi(X_i)$ is nilpotent, $\pi(G)$ is for every $G$ the value of $G$ at the tuple $(\pi(X_i))_i$ (evaluation `adicEval` with respect to the zero ideal of $L$, i.e. $\mathrm{eval}_2$ along $A\to L$), $\mathrm{comul}(\pi(X_i))$ is the value of $\Phi_i$ at the tuple $(\pi(X_j)\otimes 1,\,1\otimes\pi(X_j))_j$ (evaluation with respect to the zero ideal of $L\otimes_A L$), $\mathrm{counit}(\pi(X_i))=0$, and $\mathrm{counit}(\pi(G))$ is the constant coefficient of $G$ for every $G$.
--
--   This realises the kernel of multiplication by $n$ on a commutative formal group law as a finite free commutative and cocommutative Hopf algebra over the base, presented by the ideal generated by the $n$-division series, with the group law itself as comultiplication; nilpotence of the coordinates on the quotient is assumed here rather than derived from completeness of the base. It is the variant with the zero ideal in place of a $p$-adic one, and is used in the construction of the Hopf algebra attached to a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_hopfAlgebra_surjective_ker_eq_span_nthSeries_comul_eq_adicEval_bot_of_isNilpotent.lean

